            <ArticleTitle>Diet and prevention of coronary heart disease: the potential role of phytochemicals.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>419-25</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Epidemiological studies, and some clinical trials, demonstrate that a proper diet reduces the rate of occurrence of cardiovascular disorders. Several in vitro studies suggest that some components of plant foods, most of which sharing a phenolic structure, are endowed with interesting 'pharmacological activities'. This article reviews the evidence that links a high dietary intake of phytochemicals from various sources with a reduced incidence of coronary heart disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
